<p>&nbsp;The platform brings together different applications designed to make everyday tasks easier. Its tools include a budget planner, savings tracker, habit tracker, PDF scanner, video editor, invoice creator and several other practical applications. Users can access the applications on their phones, tablets and computers through a single membership key. The service is designed to be simple to use, with applications that can be installed directly from a link rather than requiring traditional app store downloads. Once installed, they can be accessed like ordinary applications.</p>
<p>&nbsp;The applications are available for iPhone and iPad, Android devices, Windows computers, Mac computers and Chromebooks. Some of the tools available include Jis Flip, which converts images between JPG, PNG and WebP formats, combines images into PDFs, merges PDF files, allows users to sign documents and converts spreadsheets between Excel, CSV and JSON formats. It can also convert PDF pages into images. The platform also provides money-management tools that allow users to monitor their monthly finances. For example, a displayed budget illustrates a remaining monthly balance of £1,175.50, based on a salary of £1,200 and deductions for food, transport and bills.</p>
<p>&nbsp;The service provides a straightforward installation and membership process. Users begin by choosing a membership plan or starting the free trial. They then create an account, make a secure payment through Stripe when choosing a paid plan, receive their membership key and enter it into any application they want to unlock. The applications can then be installed on iPhone and iPad, Android, Windows, Mac and Chromebook devices. Users can also enable synchronisation across their devices, manage their subscription after the trial and change their plan, payment card or cancellation settings whenever necessary. The installation process is presented as a sequence of eleven steps, beginning with choosing a plan and ending with managing or cancelling the membership.</p>
<p>&nbsp;Customers can choose between three paid membership options. The monthly subscription costs £7.99, the six-month subscription costs £39.99 and the annual subscription costs £59.99. The annual plan is described as the best-value option. Users can begin with a seven-day free trial without providing a credit card. During the trial, they can access all applications, synchronisation and backup features. After the trial, they can either choose a paid plan or keep three applications of their choice free forever. The trial does not require a card, and the service states that nothing is charged during the trial and there is nothing to cancel if users decide not to continue.</p>
<p>&nbsp;A single membership key unlocks every application offered by pocketapps.store across the user's devices. Customers can open an application directly in their browser or install it on their home screen or computer desktop. The first four applications highlighted on the website are Jis Flip, Jis Lock, Jis Till and Jis Bill. Jis Flip provides private file conversion and PDF tools, including image conversion, photo resizing and compression. Jis Lock is designed for private notes, reminders, money records and diary entries, with PIN protection, strong encryption, searchable notes and the ability to pin important information. Jis Till is a small-business sales, credit and stock book that allows shop owners to record sales and expenses quickly and synchronise information across devices using encryption. Jis Bill provides a way to create invoices and quotations as PDFs on a phone, with automatic invoice numbering and encrypted synchronisation.</p>
<p>&nbsp;The free trial includes access to all applications, synchronisation and backup. Once the trial ends, users can retain three applications of their choice without paying or select one of the available membership plans. The paid options include the monthly plan at £7.99, the six-month plan at £39.99, equivalent to £6.67 per month, and the annual plan at £59.99, equivalent to £5.00 per month. The annual subscription offers a stated saving of 37%, while the six-month option offers a saving of 17%. Paid membership includes every application, including new applications introduced in the future, access across phones, tablets and computers, synchronisation and backup between devices, email reminders before renewals and the ability to cancel online in under a minute.</p>
<p>&nbsp;When customers choose a paid plan, they are required to agree to the membership terms and acknowledge the privacy policy. The plan begins immediately, and payment is taken on the day of purchase. Customers also request immediate access to the service and understand that their membership renews automatically until cancelled. Under the stated refund policy, anyone cancelling within 14 days after making a payment must pay for the period during which the service was used. Payments are processed securely through Stripe. Prices are displayed in pounds sterling for UK customers, while customers outside the UK are shown their local currency and any applicable local taxes at checkout. Customers who prefer to try the service first can use the seven-day trial without entering card details.</p>
